  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A point mass enters a gravitational field with horizontal velocity. The gravitational equipotential surfaces are shown for the field. </p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>Which of the following statements correctly describes the path of the point mass after it has entered the field?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\">A line curving upwards.</li>\n<li data-label=\"B\">A line curving downwards.</li>\n<li data-label=\"C\">A horizontal straight line.</li>\n<li data-label=\"D\">A straight line at a non-zero angle to the horizontal.</li>\n</ol>"
  },
